{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":348221,"duration_api_ms":348165,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications accessible to implementers. This project derives specs from C source code, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies correctness through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (one package per utility), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (platform syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `magefiles/` (build targets), and `docs/` (specs, PRDs, use cases).\n\n**Current implementation**: Source code exists for all foundational packages and three utilities:\n- `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format` — complete (rel00.0)\n- `cmd/version` — complete (rel00.0)\n- `cmd/wc` — complete (rel01.0)\n- `cmd/cat` — complete (rel01.1)\n- `cmd/sponge` — complete (rel01.2)\n\n**Next release**: rel01.3 — `cmd/du` (du specification and differential test). Specs are complete; code generation has not started. No source code exists for `cmd/du`.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nReleases rel00.0 through rel01.2 are effectively complete (source code exists for all use cases). The earliest incomplete release in scope is **rel01.3** with use case `rel01.3-uc001-du`. The du PRD, use case, and test suite are all spec-complete. The implementation depends on `pkg/sys.Lstat` (for `Blocks`, `Dev`, `Ino` fields) and `pkg/format.HumanSize` (for human-readable output), both of which already exist. No blockers.\n\nPer P2, implementation and tests are separate tasks. Per P8, implementation before tests. The single task proposed is the `cmd/du/main.go` implementation.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/du: Core implementation (prd008-du R1, R2, R3, R5)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd008-du.yaml (du PRD with all requirements and acceptance criteria -- if this file does not exist, glob for prd*-du.yaml in docs/specs/product-requirements/)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.3-uc001-du.yaml (du end-to-end execution path)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.3.yaml (du test cases with inputs and expected outputs -- if not found, search docs/specs/test-suites/ for a file matching *01.3* or *du*)\n      - cmd/wc/main.go (reference single-file implementation pattern for a cmd/ utility)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo.go (Lstat function and FileInfo struct with Blocks, Dev, and Ino fields)\n      - pkg/format/size.go (HumanSize function for human-readable size formatting)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/du/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: du command implementation with flag parsing, recursive directory traversal, size calculation, output formatting, and error handling\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement flag parsing and main entry point per the du PRD R1: define an options struct holding all flag values, parse all PRD-specified flags using flag.NewFlagSet with ContinueOnError, expand combination flags, collect file/directory arguments (default to current directory '.' when none given), and call run() which returns 0 on success or 1 on error\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement recursive directory traversal with disk usage accumulation per the du PRD R2: walk each argument path using os.ReadDir and pkg/sys.Lstat, accumulate FileInfo.Blocks (512-byte units) for each file and directory, respect -x (stay on one filesystem by comparing FileInfo.Dev), -L/-P (symlink following via os.Stat vs pkg/sys.Lstat), --max-depth pruning, -S (separate directory accounting that excludes subdirectory sizes from parent totals), and track hard links by FileInfo.Ino to avoid double-counting files with Nlink > 1\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement output formatting per the du PRD R3: print size and path per entry (one line per directory by default), convert 512-byte block counts to the requested display unit (default 1024-byte blocks for -k, apparent byte size for -b/--apparent-size using FileInfo.Size, arbitrary --block-size=N), use pkg/format.HumanSize with Binary=true for -h and Binary=false for --si, print grand total line with -c, control which entries appear via -a (all files) / -s (summary only) / --max-depth, and use NUL line terminator when -0 is active\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement error handling and exit codes per the du PRD R5: print per-file errors to stderr in 'du: <path>: <error>' format using os.PathError unwrapping (matching the pattern in cmd/wc printFileError and cmd/sponge printError), continue processing remaining arguments after per-file errors, exit 0 when all arguments succeed, exit 1 when any error occurs, and install a SIGPIPE signal handler that exits cleanly\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the single-file cmd/ pattern established by cmd/wc and cmd/sponge: main.go contains main(), run(args []string) int, an options struct, and all helper functions\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use pkg/sys.Lstat (not os.Stat or os.Lstat directly) for all file metadata to access the Blocks, Dev, and Ino fields needed for disk usage calculation, cross-device detection, and hard-link deduplication\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Use pkg/format.HumanSize with HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true} for -h flag and HumanSizeOpts{Binary: false} for --si flag\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Use flag.NewFlagSet(\\\"du\\\", flag.ContinueOnError) with fs.SetOutput(os.Stderr), matching the flag parsing pattern in cmd/wc and cmd/sponge\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: cmd/du/main.go compiles successfully with go build ./cmd/du/\n      - id: AC2\n        text: All flags specified in the du PRD are defined in the flag set and accepted without error\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Default behavior with no flags and a directory argument recursively reports disk usage in 1024-byte blocks for each subdirectory and the argument itself\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Exit codes match PRD specification: 0 on full success, 1 when any file or directory produces an error\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: Error messages printed to stderr match the GNU gdu format for the same error condition\n      - id: AC6\n        text: Implementation imports pkg/sys for Lstat and pkg/format for HumanSize -- does not duplicate syscall logic or size formatting\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"d062a117-7083-4857-bb9a-7e55a97f844c","total_cost_usd":0.48831500000000005,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":95810,"output_tokens":17616,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":17616,"cacheReadInputTokens":95810,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.48831500000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"3471b2f3-f114-4e3c-996b-0490747e97e3"}
